          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            We discuss (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoBinarySullivanDifferentialIsWhiteheadProduct"}
            below) how the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+product"} Whitehead product
            is the co-binary part of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan differential
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
          %h2#notation_and_conventions Notation and conventions
          %p We make explicit some notation and normalization conventions that enter the statement.
          %p
            In the following, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+module"} graded module
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi W
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi Sym
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi β
                  %mo ∼
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mi β
                  %mi β
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  W \wedge W
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  Sym^2(W)
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\big(
                  W \otimes W
                  \\big)
                  \/
                  \\big(
                  \\alpha \otimes \beta
                  \\sim
                  (-1)^{ n_\alpha n_\beta }
                  \\beta \otimes \alpha
                  \\big)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the right
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %mi β
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha, \beta \in W
            are elements of homogeneous degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi n
